==Powers and Abilities==
<gallery type="slideshow">
TFKC (131).png|Enhanced Speed/Quadrupedalism
TFKC (148).png|Camouflage
Chamalien Enhanced Strength.png|Enhanced Strength
</gallery>
Chamalien's main ability is his camouflage, as he is capable of blending in with the color of his surroundings with such effectiveness that he appears invisible.

Chamalien is very agile, quick, flexible, and can climb walls and crawl on the ground with ease.<ref>''[[The Flame Keepers' Circle]]''</ref> He also has teeth and claws which are sharp enough to damage [[Exo-Skull|Exo-Skull]]'s armor, as demonstrated by [[Subdora]].<ref name="TEoaE">''[[The End of an Era]]''</ref>

Chamalien has a long, retractable black stinger that can come out of the tip of his tail; this feat was exclusively demonstrated by [[Prisoner 775]].<ref name="PN775IM" />

Chamalien has enhanced strength, enough to push a car and a huge truck several yards away and defeat a [[Vulpimancer (Classic)|Vulpimancer]] in battle. He is also durable enough to withstand being thrown against a car; both of these feats were also only demonstrated by Prisoner 775.<ref name="PN775IM" />

Chamalien's body is highly slippery and smooth, making him very difficult to grab.<ref name="PN775IM" />

==Weaknesses==
[[File:NotLN (319).png|thumb|Trackable Footprints]]
Although Chamalien appears to turn invisible when he camouflages himself, he actually just changes his color. Consequently, his shadow can still be seen, and any place filled with too many bright lights can be a disadvantage, as demonstrated with Prisoner 775.<ref name="PN775IM" />

Chamalien can easily be tracked by [[Vulpimancer (Classic)|Vulpimancer]]s using their enhanced senses, as demonstrated with [[Prisoner 775]]<ref name="PN775IM" /> and [[Subdora]].<ref name="FatM">''[[Fight at the Museum]]''</ref> He can also be tracked by [[Anodite|Anodites]] through his [[manna]].<ref name="NotLN">''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]''</ref>

Chamalien's camouflage can also be rendered useless if he is either carrying something or coated in another material such as powder<ref name="FatM" /> or oil,<ref name="LDtTWA">''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]''</ref> as demonstrated with [[Subdora]].

Chamalien can be controlled and hypnotized by [[Vladat]]s via their [[Corruptura]]s, as also demonstrated with Subdora.<ref name="TEoaE" />

==History==
===Ultimate Alien===
*Chamalien first appeared in ''[[Prisoner Number 775 is Missing]]'', where he was obtained by scanning [[Prisoner 775]]'s DNA and tried out by [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]].
*In ''[[The Flame Keepers' Circle]]'', Chamalien snuck into a building controlled by the [[Flame Keepers' Circle]].
*In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', Chamalien appeared twice in a dream. Firstly, Ben as Chamalien ran away from [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] and hid in the woods until he reverted. Later, [[Albedo|Negative]] Chamalien ambushed Ben before switching into Negative [[Big Chill (Classic)|Big Chill]].

