==Etymology==
Chamalien's name is portmanteau of "[[Wikipedia:Chameleon|chameleon]]", an animal capable of changing its color, which alludes to his ability to camouflage himself, and "[[Wikipedia:Extraterrestrial life|alien]]", a reference to Chamalien being an extraterrestrial life form, as well as a transformation.

==Trivia==
*Chamalien speaks with a light [[Wikipedia:Germany|German]] accent.
*When [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] first transformed into Chamalien, he named the form Overkill as a joke.<ref name="PN775IM" /> In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', his name Chamalien was first mentioned, albeit in [[Albedo]]'s nightmare, meaning his real name has never been acknowledged by Ben himself.
*When asked what kinds of features Chamalien's helmet has, [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] compared the spectrum-wide visions to those found in helmets worn by [[Wikipedia:Predator (fictional species)|Yautja]].{{Refn|[[:File:Chamalien Helmet Features.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Chamalien was revealed in a picture released on the [http://www.facebook.com/ben10 '''Ben 10''' Facebook page] on April 17, 2011, as a reward for hitting 1,000,000 fans.{{Refn|group = FB|name = page}}
*Chamalien had concept art drawn by [[Glen Murakami]]. His final design was created by [[Glenn Wong]], with color styling by Chris Hooten.{{Refn|https://archive.is/hySfU|group = GW}}
*Chamalien was not originally supposed to appear in:
**In ''[[The Flame Keepers' Circle]]'' with Ben sneaking in the the [[Flame Keepers' Circle]] headquarters in human form.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/6/66/TFKC_Script_First_Draft.pdf ''Keepers of the Flame'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = script 1}}{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/4/4c/TFKC_Script_Second_Draft.pdf ''Keepers of the Flame'' Script Second Draft]|group = script|name = script 2}}{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/f/f9/TFKC_Script_Third_Draft.pdf ''Keepers of the Flame'' Script Third Draft]|group = script}}
**The dream in ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', used by Ben and Albedo.{{Refn|[https://web.archive.org/web/20250621100125/https://dwaynemcduffie.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/WEBSITE-B10UA-ep317-Night-of-the-Living-Nightmare-SCRIPT-D1.pdf ''Night of the Living Nightmare'' Script First Draft]|group = script}}
*In ''[[Universe vs. Tennyson]]'', it was initially planned that Ben would use Chamalien to spy on [[Chadzmuth]],{{Refn|[[:File:Chamalien's dropped scene in 058.PNG]]|group = DJW}} but the whole scene was eventually dropped as the story was changed.{{Refn|[[:File:Story was changed in 058.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
**As a result of this, Chamalien and [[Fasttrack]] are the only regular aliens introduced in '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' who do not appear in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]'''.
**Additionally, Chamalien and [[Spitter]] are the only regular aliens to not get a verbal mention throughout '''Omniverse'''.
**Had Chamalien appeared in '''Omniverse''', Derrick would have chosen [[Dee Bradley Baker]] to reprise his role.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Spitter & Chamalien Voices.png]]|group = DJW}}
*There were no plans to feature Chamalien in the [[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|Reboot]].{{Refn|[[:File:RB No Spitter or Chamalien.png]]|group = DR}}

